---
title: Quiche Lorraine
description: A classic French savory tart with a rich custard filling, smoky bacon, and tender onions.
servings: 4
prep time: 25 minutes
cook time: 45 minutes
tags:
  - mains
  - french
  - classic
source: https://www.tantefanny.com/rezepte/quiche-lorraine
---

= Preparation

Preheat the oven to 190°C (375°F). 

Grease a #tart tin{} with @unsalted butter{1%tsp}. Unroll the @quiche dough{300%g} and place it into the tin, pressing it firmly against the bottom and sides. Use any overhanging dough to reinforce the edges.

= Filling

In a #mixing bowl{}, whisk together @large eggs{4}, @crème fraîche{150%g}, and chopped @fresh parsley{1%tbsp}. 

Season the mixture with @ground nutmeg{1%pinch}, @cayenne pepper{1%pinch}, @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp}, and freshly ground @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.

= Assembly & Baking

Scatter @bacon{250%g}(diced) and @onion{1}(sliced into rings) evenly over the base of the dough.

Pour the egg and crème fraîche mixture over the bacon and onions.

Place the quiche on the lowest rack of the oven and bake for ~{45%minutes} until the filling is set and the top is golden brown.
